# Fraud Detection using Machine Learning

## DecodeLabs Industrial Training — Project 2

### Supervised Learning: Fraud Detection Pipeline

**Objective:**  
Build and tune machine learning classification models to identify fraudulent transactions in a highly imbalanced dataset.

### Models Used
- Logistic Regression
- Random Forest Classifier

### Techniques Used
- Data Preprocessing
- Train-Test Split
- SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique)
- Scikit-Learn Pipelines
- Hyperparameter Tuning using GridSearchCV

### Evaluation Metrics
- Precision
- Recall
- ROC-AUC
- Confusion Matrix

> **Note:** Accuracy is not used as the primary evaluation metric because fraud detection datasets are highly imbalanced.
